From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: speed dial on letter keys

BlackBerry speed dial: each letter A-Z can hold one number.

* Phone main screen (dial pad closed, no text field focused): holding a
  plain letter calls its number through PreCall, so SIM choice and
  emergency handling are Phone's own. A letter with no number opens the
  speed dial list and the contact picker for it. A short press keeps its
  list meaning (contacts A-Z jump); the hold's later repeats and release
  are swallowed.
* Menu > Speed dial lists A to Z: Enter picks a contact's number for a
  letter, or offers Call, Choose another contact and Remove; a letter
  key moves to its row.
* Sable Start: SableSpeedDialProvider (org.sableos.dialer.speeddial)
  returns the assigned letters only, never numbers or names, and
  SableSpeedDialCallActivity (action org.sableos.dialer.action.SPEED_DIAL)
  places the call, both behind the signature permission
  org.sableos.permission.SPEED_DIAL, so Start needs no call permission.

The list is Phone's own preferences file. Pure rules:
sable/SableSpeedDial.java.
